                <pb facs="0541" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13821: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-23T12:00:00+08:00">December 23,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 23—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>633. Nanking’s 372, December 22, midnight [<hi rendition="#italic">noon?</hi>]. A
                    representative of the Military Attaché’s office, probably Colonel Stilwell
                    himself, will leave for Loyang tonight. I told Colonel Stilwell that he should
                    strongly urge evacuation of American citizens from Shensi if evacuation is
                    possible.</p>
                <p>Nanking and Shanghai informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
